# dev-guardian (MCP)

This project has the dev-guardian MCP server registered. ~50 tools and 16
resources for security, quality, bugfix, deps, compliance, observability,
performance, plus first-class WordPress and .NET (C#/F#) support. All
scanners run locally, no telemetry, results persisted in
`.guardian/guardian.db`.

**Prefer these MCP tools over invoking scanners directly** — you'd lose
diff_scans, baselines, suppressions, and the regression history.

## Intent → MCP tool

### Security
- "is this safe?" → `security_scan_full`
- "secrets?" → `scan_secrets`
- "CVEs?" → `scan_deps` / `deps_audit`
- "Dockerfile / container" → `scan_containers`
- "IaC" → `scan_iac`
- "deep bug hunt" → `bug_hunt`

### Quality
- "review before PR" → `review_pr`
- "code quality" → `quality_check`

### Deps
- "upgrade plan" → `deps_update_plan` (npm/pip/composer/cargo/go/bundler/dotnet)
- "audit deps" → `deps_audit`

### Compliance
- "GDPR / SOC2 / ISO27001" → `compliance_check` + `compliance_evidence`
- "SBOM" → `generate_sbom`
- "license compatibility" → `license_compatibility`

### Ops
- "bootstrap" → `init_project`
- "install scanners" → `install_toolchain`
- "detect stack" → `detect_stack`
- "logging / metrics" → `observability_setup`
- "performance" → `perf_check`

### WordPress
- "scan WP code" → `scan_wordpress`
- "audit live WP" → `wp_audit`
- "WP CVEs?" → `wp_vuln_check`
- "WP cron backdoor?" → `wp_cron_audit`
- "WP REST exposed?" → `wp_rest_audit`
- "WP posture" → `wp_describe_setup`
- "hardening checklist" → `wp_recommend_hardening`
- "check plugin X" → `wp_plugin_check`
- "audit N sites" → `bulk_audit_wordpress_sites`

### .NET / C#
- ".NET secrets" → `scan_dotnet_secrets`
- "EOL frameworks" → `dotnet_target_framework_check`
- "EF Core migrations" → `dotnet_efcore_audit`
- ".NET posture" → `dotnet_describe_setup`

### Meta
- "full audit" → `audit_executive` (stack-aware)
- "risk score" → `risk_score`
- "what's new?" → `diff_scans`
- "set baseline" → `set_baseline`
- "false positives" → `triage_findings`
- "prioritise" → `prioritize_findings`
- "fix help" → `suggest_fix`
- "export report" → `report_export`
- "GitHub issues" → `create_github_issues`
- "pre-commit hooks" → `precommit_install`
- "custom Semgrep rules" → `register_custom_rules`
- "health" → `health_status`
- "regression" → `regression_alert`
- "SBOM diff" → `sbom_diff`
- "set up another AI host" → run `node bin/dev-guardian.mjs mcp-config <host>` (CLI)

## Resources

`guardian://findings/open|critical|by-severity/{level}` (paginated),
`guardian://scans/{latest|history|id}`, `guardian://cves/active`,
`guardian://sbom`, `guardian://stack`, `guardian://compliance/status`,
`guardian://baseline`, `guardian://wp/{audit/latest|audit/{id}|cron}`,
`guardian://dotnet/{target-frameworks|efcore}`.

## Workflows

1. Bootstrap: detect_stack → init_project → install_toolchain →
   security_scan_full (or scan_wordpress) → set_baseline
2. Before PR: review_pr → triage_findings → prioritize_findings → suggest_fix
3. Audit: audit_executive (stack-aware) → risk_score → compliance_evidence

## Anti-patterns

- Don't `security_scan_full` for tiny changes — use review_pr
- Don't suppress_finding before triage_findings
- Don't shell out to scanners — lose persistence + baselines
- Don't run scan_wordpress on non-WP — detect_stack first
